begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -7 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -8 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+(-7)\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+(-8)\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =(-7)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-8)\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -9 & 4\\end{aligned}|-8\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77808/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77808"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5182"] :question/problem "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-6)\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+1\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4418"] :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "The $4$th row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3 \\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-8)+(0-0) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4419"] :question/problem "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
